&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This position can work onsite or hybrid from one of our offices or fully remote in the US.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 40%&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1798&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IonQ is building the world’s first fully-expressive, full-stack quantum computer based on trapped ion technology.&amp;nbsp; Quantum computing is poised to reshape medicine, materials, simulation, and much more.&amp;nbsp; To support our rapid growth, we’re hiring creative collaborators with top skills in their areas of expertise and a commitment to success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Account Executive - US Federal - Space Force that will be part of our US Federal Go-To-Market team whose mission is to bring IonQ’s offering—including Quantum Hardware (Systems and Networks), Software, Applications, and Access—to a curated set of clients across the US Department of War. This is an individual contributor role with potential to build a team down the road.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Space, Land, and T&amp;amp;E Partnerships: Cultivate and maintain executive-level relationships within the U.S. Space Force (e.g., Space Systems Command, Space RCO), U.S. Army (e.g., AFC, PEO IEW&amp;amp;S, PEO STRI), and the Test Resource Management Center (TRMC). Work in lockstep with your Field Engineer counterpart to align IonQ solutions with specific requirements, such as the Army’s Multi-Domain Operations (MDO) and USSF’s Space Warfighting Analysis Center (SWAC) initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-Focused Pipeline Generation: Develop a robust pipeline of opportunities across IonQ’s full stack, specifically targeting:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantum Computing for satellite constellation optimization, Army tactical logistics, and high-fidelity T&amp;amp;E modeling and simulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantum Networking for secure Space-to-Ground communications, cross-domain data sharing, and resilient tactical networks for the modular Army.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantum Sensing for PNT in contested space environments, subterranean/urban sensing for ground forces, and advanced instrumentation for TRMC test ranges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Qualification and Mission Alignment: Prioritize opportunities based on their potential for enhancing orbital security, ground force lethality, and T&amp;amp;E infrastructure modernization. Navigate RDT&amp;amp;E accounts and transition technologies into Programs of Record (PoR), ensuring alignment with the Army’s 2030/2040 Transformation and the Space Force’s vision for a resilient space order of battle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full Lifecycle Capture Management: Own the end-to-end sales and capture lifecycle. This includes navigating the federal acquisition process, leading technical qualifications, and managing formal RFI/RFP responses. Execute complex negotiations for defense-specific vehicles, including OTAs, SBIR/STTR Phase II/III, and TRMC-specific funding streams (e.g., Central Test and Evaluation Investment Program).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Command: Mobilize and lead internal IonQ teams—including Security (clearing FOCI concerns), Legal, and Engineering—to provide the technical depth and compliance required to win high-stakes USSF, Army, and TRMC contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational and Range Integration: Partner with delivery and support teams post-award to ensure seamless integration into the warfighter&#39;s workflow and T&amp;amp;E range environments. Drive long-term adoption, facilitate contract renewals, and identify expansion opportunities for new mission sets across the Space and Land domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defense GTM Tenure: Minimum of 10 years of experience selling to the Department of the Army, U.S. Space Force, or OSD-level agencies (like TRMC) with quota-carrying responsibilities and a proven ability to close multi-million dollar platform or infrastructure deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HPC and Mission Infrastructure Sales: Experience selling high-performance computing (HPC), AI/ML infrastructure, or advanced mission systems (hardware or software) to the Department of Defense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USSF, Army, and T&amp;amp;E Network: Existing relationships within the U.S. Space Force (e.g., SSC, Starcom), U.S. Army (e.g., Army Futures Command, DEVCOM, PEO Soldier), and/or TRMC, with a deep understanding of their unique mission sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complex Federal GTM Problem Solving: Ability to navigate the unique federal procurement process, security compliance requirements (including FedRAMP and IL levels), and National Security hurdles. Proven ability to move technologies through the T&amp;amp;E phase and into Programs of Record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Targeted Senior Level Relationships: Existing senior-level relationships (e.g., PEOs, Lab Directors, or Chief Scientists) within Space Systems Command (SSC), Army DEVCOM, or the TRMC leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain Expertise: Deep understanding of USSF and Army operational drivers that can be enhanced using Quantum, such as orbital mechanics, satellite resilience, electromagnetic spectrum operations (EMSO), and T&amp;amp;E range instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI/ML for Defense: Experience selling AI/ML, high-performance analytics, or autonomous systems solutions for use by space operators, ground commanders, or test and evaluation engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantum Literacy: Knowledge of Quantum technologies (Compute, Networks, and Sensing) specifically as they relate to DoD applications, such as quantum-secure satellite links, subterranean mapping, and ultra-precise T&amp;amp;E data collection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Category Creation: Experience in category creation selling—specifically creating compelling approaches to sell frontier technology solutions that are not yet established Programs of Record or standard line items in RDT&amp;amp;E or TRMC budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OTE for this role is expected to be $380K&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base, commission, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Wage Transparency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$182,400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$262,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role will work onsite at our office located in Bothell, WA.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 5%, domestic or international.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1877&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Buyer Planner to join our Supply Chain team. As a Buyer Planner, you&#39;ll be part of a cross-functional team whose mission is to lead IonQ on its journey to build the world&#39;s best quantum computers to solve the world&#39;s most complex problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the buy side of the material plan — converting demand into purchase orders, holding vendors to committed dates, and keeping the supply picture in the ERP accurate enough that the rest of the organization can plan against it. You are the connection point between what the factory needs and what the supply base has actually agreed to deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-volume, high-judgment execution role. Lead times are long, demand shifts, and a large share of what you buy is custom or single-source. The ideal candidate is someone who works a queue with discipline, chases commitments rather than replies, and understands that a date is only real once it is recorded in the system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Purchasing Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review the buyer workbench daily for new demand, pull-ins, quantity changes, and cancellations before releasing anything, so that every release is a deliberate decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release compressed lead time purchase requests first, prioritizing items past the Suggested Order Date, then batch standard within-lead-time releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create Transfer Orders to connect supply and demand across locations and subsidiaries, checking other locations&#39; on-hand before releasing a new PO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work the purchase request intake queue end to end: requests assigned to you, items needing a vendor or vendor part number, quote requests, returned or rejected requests, and approved requests with no PO created yet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Return a status note to the requester on anything aging in the queue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Delivery &amp;amp; Supplier Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chase purchase order acknowledgments where a vendor has not confirmed price, quantity, and date&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm delivery dates and update the PO with each new committed date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive expedite and pull-in requests for material creating a shortage or a compressed date;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Data Integrity &amp;amp; Financial Accuracy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve three-way match discrepancies — price variance, quantity variance, or missing receipts — correcting whichever record is actually wrong rather than forcing the invoice through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain lead times in NetSuite for items missing them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and load preferred vendors and vendor part numbers for items missing them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[2]+ years of purchasing, buying, or materials planning experience in a manufacturing environment, or an equivalent combination of education and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Supply Chain, Operations, Business, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MRP/ERP purchasing mechanics — planned orders, suggested order dates, lead time logic, exception messages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing vendor relationships and holding suppliers to committed delivery dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills — pivot tables, lookups, and the ability to build a working analysis without waiting on a report request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret BOMs and engineering drawings well enough to buy the right part&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and persistent; able to work a large daily queue to completion and communicate status clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NetSuite or a comparable Tier 1/Tier 2 ERP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with an intake or procure-to-pay tool such as Zip, Coupa, or Ariba&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-mix / low-volume, prototype-to-production, or new product introduction environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APICS/ASCM certification (CPIM, CPSM, CSCP) or active pursuit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience buying custom fabrication, machined parts, electronics, or long-lead capital equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with three-way match, receiving, and AP resolution workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of business analytics reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Wage Transparency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$126,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
