&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based at our Santa Clara, CA office, with the option to work a few days a week remotely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 15%, domestic or international.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1903&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Frontend Engineer with 5+/8+ years of experience to design and build the interface for our Quantum Security platform. This role blends product design thinking with hands-on frontend engineering — you&#39;ll turn complex network and security data into interfaces that are intuitive, fast, and trustworthy for security and network teams. As a senior member of the team, you&#39;ll also help shape frontend architecture, mentor junior engineers, and drive design/engineering best practices. You&#39;ll work closely with product managers, backend engineers, and QA/solutions teams to ship features that make sense to real users under real operational pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement responsive, accessible UI components for the platform using modern frontend frameworks (React, Vue, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex network security concepts — topology maps, risk/posture scores, policy rules, alerts, remediation steps — into clear, usable visual interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end UX for key workflows: onboarding, network/device discovery, dashboards, drill-down investigations, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity mockups (Figma or similar) and iterate based on user feedback and usability testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with backend engineers to define and consume APIs, ensuring data-heavy views (topology graphs, tables, charts) remain performant at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with QA and Solutions Testing teams to validate that workflows behave correctly and intuitively across real customer network scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct or support usability testing and gather feedback from customers, sales engineers, and support teams to continuously refine the UX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and evolve a component/design system for consistency across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure UI meets accessibility (WCAG) and cross-browser compatibility standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor frontend performance (load times, rendering of large topology/data sets) and optimize as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and evolve frontend architecture, tooling, and coding standards across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor mid-level and junior frontend/UI engineers through code reviews, pairing, and design critiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical decisions on state management, component architecture, and performance for a growing, data-intensive platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+/8+ years of experience as a frontend engineer, UI/UX engineer, or product designer with strong coding ability, ideally on data-dense or technical SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning frontend architecture decisions and mentoring other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in modern JavaScript/TypeScript and a component-based framework (React preferred; Vue/Angular acceptable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong UX design skills — information architecture, interaction design, visual hierarchy — with a portfolio demonstrating design-to-code work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing interfaces for complex, data-heavy domains (dashboards, network/graph visualizations, security tools, DevOps tools, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with design tools such as Figma, Sketch, or Adobe XD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with REST APIs and working closely with backend teams to shape data contracts for UI needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of responsive design, accessibility standards (WCAG), and cross-browser/device compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct or contribute to usability testing and translate findings into design/engineering improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in network security, cybersecurity, or IT infrastructure SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data visualization libraries (D3.js, Recharts, Cytoscape.js, or similar) for rendering network topology and graph-based data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of Layer 2/Layer 3 networking concepts (VLANs, routing, ACLs) to better design for technical users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with design systems and component libraries at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to CI/CD pipelines and frontend testing frameworks (Jest, Playwright, Cypress).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complex network and security data is presented in ways that are immediately understandable to security/network admins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Key workflows (discovery, posture review, remediation) feel fast, guided, and low-friction even for less technical users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and engineering teams ship UI changes with confidence, backed by usability validation and a consistent design system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend architecture scales cleanly as the platform and team grow, with junior engineers leveling up under your guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Wage Transparency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$124,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$186,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based at our Bothell, WA office.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; 10% domestic or international.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1715&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic, analytical, and hands-on IT Asset Manager to take full ownership of the lifecycle, financial health, and regulatory compliance of our global IT asset portfolio. In this role, you will bridge the gap between IT operations, finance, and legal compliance. You will be responsible for defining and executing asset management strategies that optimize technology spend, mitigate contract risks, track physical and logical inventory, and ensure our environments strictly align with internal security policies and external audit guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a role focused on governance, compliance, and strategy, IonQ values a collaborative, hands-on approach. You will retain close visibility into our day-to-day operations by directly managing critical lifecycle logistics and providing basic IT helpdesk troubleshooting for our internal team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Governance, Compliance &amp;amp; Financial Optimization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Asset Governance: Establish, maintain, and enforce comprehensive policies, standards, and procedures for the end-to-end lifecycle of corporate hardware and software assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Optimization &amp;amp; Budgeting: Analyze technology spend patterns, software utilization, and hardware lifecycles to identify cost-saving opportunities. Partner with Finance and IT leadership to drive IT budget forecasting and reconcile vendor invoicing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software Asset Management (SAM): Oversee software license compliance, entitlements, and SaaS subscriptions. Audit usage metrics to proactively harvest underutilized licenses and mitigate the risk of non-compliance penalties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit Readiness: Serve as the primary point of contact for internal and external IT asset audits (e.g., software publisher audits, SOC2 Type II, CMMC). Ensure corporate asset data is accurate, auditable, and continuously compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal Holds &amp;amp; Discretion: Strictly manage and enforce Corporate Legal and Security protocols regarding hardware on active legal holds. Safely isolate, log, and preserve restricted hardware, maintaining an airtight, documented chain of custody.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Asset Lifecycle Coordination &amp;amp; Logistics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-End Tracking: Supervise and execute the physical and logical lifecycle of assets—encompassing purchasing, receiving, tagging, active deployment, harvesting upon employee offboarding, and final secure data destruction/disposal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Contract Management: Manage relationships, procurement logistics, and lease frameworks with hardware and software vendors. Maintain a rigorous contract renewal calendar to prevent operational lapses or automated cost escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Functional IT Helpdesk Troubleshooting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Triage: Directly assist the IT support team by monitoring incoming helpdesk tickets, Slack channels, or walk-up requests, providing rapid triage or basic troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access &amp;amp; Provisioning Support: Handle foundational IT tasks, including user account creation, SaaS application access provisioning, and device enrollment within our cloud directories or Mobile Device Management (MDM) suites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace Tech Support: Diagnose and resolve standard, ground-level technical issues involving operating system configurations, workplace peripherals, docking stations, and local conference room configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 5+ years of experience in IT Asset Management (ITAM), Software Asset Management (SAM), IT procurement, or IT contract governance, with a proven track record of handling multi-site corporate environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial &amp;amp; Analytical Mastery: Strong experience managing IT vendor contracts, negotiating software renewals, managing vendor relations, and building data-driven cost-optimization strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance Rigor: Demonstrated ability to handle highly confidential compliance procedures, legal hold logistics, and precise chain-of-custody documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Fundamentals: Sound hands-on understanding of enterprise IT hardware, standard client operating systems (macOS and Windows), and core SaaS ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools Expertise: Proficiency with formal ITAM, SAM, or ITSM software (e.g., ServiceNow, Snipe-IT, Jira Service Desk, Flexera, or Freshservice).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Collaboration: Exceptional interpersonal skills; ability to collaborate fluidly with Corporate Legal, Finance, internal InfoSec leads, and external software auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as IAITAM Certified IT Asset Manager (CITAM), Certified Hardware Asset Management Professional (CHAMP), or Certified Software Asset Management (CSAM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in highly regulated or high-security sectors (e.g., Aerospace, Defense, or Technology) adhering to NIST SP 800-171, CMMC, or SOC2 frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating the transition from traditional on-premise infrastructure to identity-driven cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The approximate base salary range for this position is &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;$114,750&lt;/span&gt; - &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;$150,237&lt;/span&gt;. The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
